    "id": "717e623d6fd2",
    "text": "AKGEC has a wide range of student societies and clubs under Life@AKGEC, organized into four categories: Departmental Societies: Conatus (CSE), Nirmaan (IT — note: also referred to as Nirman), Oorja, Phoenix (ECE), Samveg (Mechanical Engineering). Horizon is the Departmental Society of Applied Sciences & Humanities, and Parivridhi is the Departmental Society of the MCA department. Extra-Curricular Societies: Euphony, Footprints, Horizon, Goonj, Renaissance, Taal (dance society), Verve, Photography and Media Club, and the Sports Club. Student Chapters: CSI (Computer Society of India), Indian Concrete Institute, Robotics Club (formed 8 May 2013), IEEE Communication Society Student Branch Chapter (est. April 2022, under ECE department), ISTE (Indian Society for Technical Education — a professional organization of academicians, faculty, and students across engineering colleges promoting higher studies and technical education), and SAE India. Technical Clubs: Electronics Club (helps students learn about electronics, coordinated by ECE faculty) and Communication Club (organizes seminars like \"IoT Unplugged\", under ECE department). Beyond societies, Life@AKGEC also covers Events (college-wide events), Social Responsibilities (Green Audit, National Cadet Corps, Unnat Bharat Abhiyaan & NSS, Experts Talks/Workshops, Nature Club, Adarsh Vikas Kendra,",
